{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1354975-repliciating-true-faith-effects-with-chorister-mage","id":1354975,"title":"Repliciating True Faith effects with Chorister mage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-15T03:18:12-08:00","id":1354975,"title":"Repliciating True Faith effects with Chorister mage","content":"What spheres could be used to replicate some TF (VTM) effects? I.E: Making vampires fearful and loathsome upon hearing you recite holy words and being in your presence, which also causes them to flee or risk being reduced to gibbering balls of fear (TF 5), making vampires takes a few steps back &amp; warding them off with a holy symbol (assuming some level of correspondence?), using holy symbol to cause agg (i'm guessing prime 2?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T17:56:55-08:00","id":1355095,"title":"","content":"The question is why does True Faith effect vampires in a particular way. Its easy enough to replicate particular effects(fear, damage) directly but there quite variety of INDIRECT methods. High levels of Matter and forces would let you litterally forge a sunbeam into a sword then for all intents and purposes that sword is.. the sun and kindred react thusly. There's also of course the much easier &quot;I Set my holy symbol on fire&quot; and that's going to cause a vampire to go running.<br /> <br /> The question therefore becomes how much the Beast reacts to other things.. if you charge a holy symbol with prime does it recoil or not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T05:59:00-08:00","id":1355164,"title":"","content":"True Faith is, in certain books (like the Revised Chorister Tradition book or M20), given broad license to perform &quot;miracles&quot;. It's not just interacting with vampires, though that's liable to come up in a campaign that utilizes the other splats.<br /> <br /> The following are notes about advantages True Faith can give or Effects it can perform, and how they might translate into Sphere Effects. Miracles referenced are from M20 p. 645:<ul><li>Every dot of True Faith adds to the character's Willpower dice pools. For the purposes of defending against mental Effects or powers, Mind 1 can simulate this by creating a mind shield that subtracts from the successes of such powers.</li> <li>Every dot of True Faith adds dice to countermagic rolls. Normally, countermagic is performed by a contested Arete roll (assuming the character has at least one dot in a relevant Sphere), with success on that roll subtracting successes from the Effect. With Prime, though, the character can spend Quintessence to raise the difficulty of the opposing Effect, making it harder to pull off (though how many Quint can be spent is limited by per-turn Quint expenditure, and by the number of successes on the Arete roll). Given how useful Prime is for countermagic, it's no wonder the Celestial Chorus specializes in it.</li> <li>&quot;Healing&quot; is obvious: Life 2 for oneself, Life 3 for others.</li> <li>&quot;Intersession&quot; is a broad category of miracles, involving working to fix bad conditions or mollify the &quot;powers that be&quot;. For curing the sick or dying, see the above. For &quot;forgiving sins&quot;, the ST has final say as to whether a Mage can do anything (it may be up only to the Powers That Be and/or the perpetrator, although the unclean Resonance of a terrible act could be washed away with Prime. Contacting &quot;God&quot; or otherwise making communication with the Powers That Be could possibly be done with Spirit, though whether it's actually God or a powerful Umbrood claiming to be is anyone's guess. (Although if interceding with a powerful Umbrood is the operative goal - like a person is being tormented by angry spirits - then Spirit works fine to establish communications; getting the spirits to stop is another matter, more the province of Chiminige and roleplay than Sphere Effects). Entropy can undo curses, and bring good luck to someone about to engage in dangerous activity.</li> <li>&quot;Penance&quot; - making a character feel remorse for their actions and repent - can be attempted with Mind. Either forcing the character to feel bad, giving them the clarity of vision to understand the weight of their transgressions, or actually mind-controlling someone in repenting. In the latter case, the Effect will probably be temporary, and might not &quot;count&quot; as far as redeeming someone goes, since they didn't choose penance freely.</li> <li>&quot;Shielding&quot; is another group of functions that have different particular Spheres governing them. Protecting from natural forces like fire or weapons could be done with Forces shields, while Life 3 (Life 4 for others) could allow for the soaking of damage (and even in boosting Stamina stats temporarily). Correspondence can create Wards and Bans, with conjunctional Spheres used to hedge out certain kinds of things. As stated earlier, Mind can create a mental shield against psychic effects, and could possibly be used to retreat into oneself to endure the effects of torture or other forms of suffering. Even Spirit can protect against spiritual effects, by strengthening the local Gauntlet.</li> <li>&quot;Transmutation&quot; involves using the various pattern Spheres - Forces, Life, and Matter - to change one thing into another. In the case of negating poisons in the body, Life + Matter is the way to go.</li> <li>Vampires can be stopped or driven off by Mind, through instilling fear, guilt, or existential/religious horror, or by outright mind controlling the leech. Mind + Correspondence can be used to create a Ward (whether around the Mage or at a fixed location) that instills the aforementioned emotions into any vampire in proximity. As stated with Shielding, a Ban against vampires can be made, using Correspondence + Life + Matter (to Ban their bodies) or Correspondence + Mind (to Ban anyone with the vampiric mindset, or who identifies as a blood-drinker).</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T03:58:31-08:00","id":1355357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1354975-repliciating-true-faith-effects-with-chorister-mage#post1354975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What spheres could be used to replicate some TF (VTM) effects? I.E: Making vampires fearful and loathsome upon hearing you recite holy words and being in your presence, which also causes them to flee or risk being reduced to gibbering balls of fear (TF 5), making vampires takes a few steps back &amp; warding them off with a holy symbol (assuming some level of correspondence?), using holy symbol to cause agg (i'm guessing prime 2?)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmmm, it really depends. using words to banish them is Mind, warding is Space/Corr. and aggro with holy symbol is Prime. <br /> <br /> However, you can copy all of these and more with Spirit. Talens and Fetishes (more suited for hermetics) of angels would work <i>wonders </i>on any vampire. Those <i>should </i>also automatically count as relics to be fair, with their own true faith scores, you are literally using angel power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}